Subject: Re:  Extropian filter

In response to Keith Henson's suggestion that VR is the hole that
all civilizations fall into:  

If you have been converted into digital form, then the natural
way to travel to another star is via interstellar modem.  It can
be easily shown that the energy to send a description of an object
is many times lower than the energy to send a physical object at
a substantial fraction of C.  

All you need to do is send your nanomachines or whatever via 
robot probe to the next star, then have them build a big
receiving station.  The subjective time to travel via photons
is ZERO, no matter how fast your thinking is sped up.

